1
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:48,560
Xiao Ting, can you handle spicy food?

2
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:49,360
I can.

3
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:50,320
Add a bit more, add more.

4
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:50,880
Add more.

5
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:52,120
By the way.

6
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:52,440
Here.

7
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:53,240
Okay, that's enough.

8
00:02:57,840 --> 00:03:00,240
Xiao Mei isn't replying to my WeChat messages.

9
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:01,040
What's going on?

10
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,600
Well, it's like this.

11
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:04,320
Our place was shut down for restructuring, right?

12
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:06,160
So everyone lost their jobs.

13
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:07,800
Xiao Mei went back to her hometown in the country.

14
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:11,160
It's all my fault.

15
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:13,720
I caused everyone to lose their jobs.

16
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,080
I'll take a penalty drink.

17
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:17,120
I'll drink with you, Huilan.

18
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:23,720
Xiao Ting.

19
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:26,080
What are your plans for the future?

20
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:27,720
Me?

21
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:30,440
I've been working out here for almost half a year now.

22
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,160
And I realized...

23
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:33,840
I realized staying in school is better.

24
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:36,360
If you study,

25
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:38,520
you won't have to look for jobs like this anymore.

26
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,200
So I've decided.

27
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,560
I'm going back to study hard.

28
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:46,400
Studying is good.

29
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:48,920
You definitely need to study more.

30
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:53,120
When I was young,

31
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:55,160
I just didn't study enough.

32
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:59,040
Knowledge is a weapon.

33
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:00,520
Learn as much as you can.

34
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:01,280
Strap it to yourself.

35
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:03,480
One on the left, one on the right.

36
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:06,160
Only then will you realize

37
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:08,480
that when a girl is making her way in the world,

38
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,000
it comes in handy.

39
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:12,120
Then no one will dare to bully you.

40
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:12,920
Got it?

41
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:15,120
I got it, Huilan.

42
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,760
Thank you for everything you've done.

43
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,280
If it weren't for you,

44
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:21,320
I'd probably still be suffering in silence in that hellhole.

45
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,120
Thank you.

46
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:29,000
Stop with all that.

47
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,880
Me, I'm actually getting a bit emotional.

48
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:32,840
Hurry up and eat. It's on me today.

49
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:36,120
You're treating?

50
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:39,520
How can you treat without me?

51
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:40,240
Right?

52
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:41,880
Boss Jiang.

53
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:43,920
As soon as Huilan comes here,

54
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:45,680
you come over just to steal the spotlight.

55
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,200
Aren't you two...

56
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:48,520
both out of work now?

57
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:49,640
Right?

58
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:52,400
Come on.

59
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:54,720
Let's have a drink.

60
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:55,720
Drink up.

61
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:58,120
Aren't you embarrassed?

62
00:04:58,120 --> 00:04:59,960
What do you mean by pouring so little?

63
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:01,840
If you want to show your sincerity,

64
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:04,560
remember what Wang Daren did last time?

65
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:09,960
Chug, chug it.

66
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:15,240
Fine.

67
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:16,240
I'll chug it today.

68
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:29,720
Keep going.

69
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:30,920
Come on.

70
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:31,800
Let's do another one.

71
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,160
See?

72
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:43,920
A man like this,

73
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:45,040
how can you count on him?

74
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:47,360
That son of a bitch can't even outdrink me.

75
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:49,520
Boss Jiang is such a lightweight.

76
00:05:52,640 --> 00:05:53,480
Huilan,

77
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:58,680
I... I'm actually not very good with words.

78
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:02,640
But I really appreciate your help.

79
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:05,320
Everything I want to say is in this drink.

80
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:06,840
Thank you.

81
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:22,200
Are you heading back to your hometown tomorrow?

82
00:06:22,320 --> 00:06:23,480
You don't have to worry about me.

83
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:25,600
If I get the chance,

84
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:28,200
I'll definitely come back to visit you.

85
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:41,360
Xiao Ting.

86
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:42,120
Here.

87
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:43,840
Take this.

88
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:46,680
This is...

89
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:47,560
Huilan.

90
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:48,680
You have to take it.

91
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:49,560
No, Huilan.

92
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:52,160
Listen to me, you need to take it.

93
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:53,200
Don't...

94
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:55,160
Don't be like this.

95
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:57,120
You have to study hard.

96
00:06:57,120 --> 00:06:57,960
You hear me?

97
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:01,640
Only with a good education

98
00:07:02,080 --> 00:07:03,600
can you boldly step out into the world.

99
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:06,400
I believe

100
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:08,320
you'll definitely make a name for yourself.

101
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:18,240
I'm going to miss you so much.

102
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:19,680
Remember to come back and visit me.

103
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:23,000
You'll always be the best big sister to me.

104
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:27,040
All right.

105
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:29,520
Okay.

106
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:33,040
Face life with a smile.

107
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:35,800
I'll walk you to a cab.

108
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:36,840
Okay.

109
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:40,760
Let's go to the gate and get a ride

110
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:42,440
and head home.

111
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:50,960
Old Li.

112
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:51,960
I've got something to do.

113
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:53,320
Watch my stall for a bit.

114
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:53,960
Okay.

115
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:54,920
Don't worry.

116
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:56,320
Thanks.

117
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:02,520
Where are you going?

118
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:22,760
We're here.

119
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:29,080
Why bring me to a cornfield in the middle of the night?

120
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:30,880
Drop the act.

121
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:32,040
I know you're not drunk.

122
00:08:33,520 --> 00:08:34,520
You figured it out.

123
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:36,400
Men know men best.

124
00:08:36,720 --> 00:08:38,240
I know you're up to no good with Huilan.

125
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:39,080
I'm warning you.

126
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:40,400
Don't get any ideas about her.

127
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,840
You're quite overprotective, aren't you?

128
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:44,760
Me? Do I really look like such a bad guy?

129
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:45,880
I don't care if you look like one or not.

130
00:08:45,880 --> 00:08:47,240
Just get out of the car.

131
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:51,480
You're just gonna leave?

132
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:52,120
Wait.

133
00:08:52,120 --> 00:08:52,720
Hey!

134
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:54,520
I'm still your boss, you know.

135
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:56,640
Not after work, you're not.

136
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:59,440
Remember to return the hat tomorrow.

137
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:00,520
The hat?

138
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:01,720
Hat?

139
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:03,640
What is this place?

140
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:14,400
My...

141
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:15,880
My phone's dead too!

142
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:16,640
Hey,

143
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:17,960
wait,

144
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:18,720
don't go!

145
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:19,920
My phone's dead!

146
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:20,800
What am I supposed to do?

147
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:45,880
Li Yiran!

148
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:49,480
Come out!

149
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:50,600
Where are you?

150
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:51,720
Stop yelling.

151
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:53,560
Look at the time. You're waking the neighbors.

152
00:09:55,920 --> 00:09:57,320
I brought you some good food.

153
00:09:57,520 --> 00:09:59,080
Uncle Daren grilled it for you.

154
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,120
You drank again.

155
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:06,520
No, I didn't.

156
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:08,280
I can smell it.

157
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:09,840
Impossible.

158
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:11,360
Look how straight I'm walking.

159
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:13,600
You're always so stubborn.

160
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:18,080
I have something to tell you.

161
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:19,840
Perfect.

162
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:21,360
I have something to tell you too.

163
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:26,920
You go first then.

164
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:33,360
I got a job offer from a company in Shanghai.

165
00:10:33,920 --> 00:10:35,120
They want me to start at the end of the month.

166
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:37,280
This company...

167
00:10:37,280 --> 00:10:39,960
Is one I've always really wanted to work for.

168
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:43,400
That's great news.

169
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:46,560
But I'm still hesitating.

170
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:47,880
Why are you hesitating?

171
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:50,920
You've lived in Shanghai for so many years.

172
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:51,920
If it weren't for me...

173
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:52,960
Holding you back...

174
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:55,000
You'd have been promoted and rich there long ago.

175
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:55,640
Why hesitate?

176
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:56,400
Just go.

177
00:10:56,920 --> 00:10:58,760
I'm just afraid you'll cause trouble if I leave.

178
00:10:59,400 --> 00:11:00,560
What kind of trouble could I cause?

179
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:03,120
Me, I've got hands and feet, and I'm smart too.

180
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:04,760
I don't need you watching me every day.

181
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:05,880
You don't need me watching you?

182
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:08,000
Then let me remind you of all the messes you've made.

183
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:09,960
Hurry up and eat. Just eat.

184
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:10,560
While it's hot.

185
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:11,920
It'll get cold soon.

186
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:13,080
Here's some chili powder too.

187
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:15,920
Didn't you say you had something to tell me?

188
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:18,280
What is it?

189
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:23,680
I just wanted to tell you...

190
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:30,480
I...

191
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:31,920
Passed my probation.

192
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:35,040
My job will be stable from now on.

193
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:36,600
And my income will be stable too.

194
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:37,360
That's great.

195
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:38,400
Yeah.

196
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:41,720
You should still take my bankbook.

197
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:43,040
I don't have any use for it anyway.

198
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:44,360
When you get to Shanghai...

199
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:45,840
You'll need to rent a place...

200
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:47,000
And order takeout.

201
00:11:47,720 --> 00:11:48,520
Take it.

202
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:50,240
Is this what you wanted to say?

203
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:53,320
Just this.

204
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:55,080
No need for that.

205
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:56,800
As for your money...

206
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:57,960
Just keep it for yourself.

207
00:11:58,320 --> 00:12:00,200
I'll be making 15k a month there.

208
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:01,920
And I get double pay at the end of the year.

209
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:04,440
How much is 15k?

210
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:05,560
Fifteen thousand.

211
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:07,480
Fifteen thousand.

212
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:09,320
That much?

213
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:11,560
Then we definitely have to celebrate.

214
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:18,720
Pure draft.

215
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:19,520
You know?

216
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:21,320
I don't usually bring this out to drink.

217
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:31,240
Cheers.

218
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:46,120
Bottoms up.

219
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:52,120
That's right.

220
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:53,480
What are you saving that for?

221
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:55,760
To raise fish?

222
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:56,440
You gonna raise fish in it?

223
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:25,520
I'm heading out.

224
00:13:25,640 --> 00:13:26,840
I'm off to work.

225
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:33,240
I'll cook tonight.

226
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:34,640
Come home for dinner after work.

227
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:37,040
Alright, alright, alright.

228
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:15,720
Hurry up, hurry up!

229
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:16,800
He's crying, he's crying!

230
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:28,120
Hoeing fields in the midday sun,

231
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:30,480
Sweat drips into the soil below.

232
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:33,760
Hoeing fields in the midday sun,

233
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:35,600
Ugly freak!

234
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:37,480
Give me candy!

235
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:43,200
Who knows that the food on our plates,

236
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:46,600
Every grain comes from hard work.

237
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:49,720
Who knows that the food on our plates,

238
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:50,760
Ugly freak!

239
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:13,040
Well, uh...

240
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:21,640
your luck...

241
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:23,640
I'm sorry.

242
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:42,920
You don't have a job anymore. Why are you out all day?

243
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:44,760
Now that I don't have a job,

244
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:45,760
pretending to have one...

245
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:47,200
is what's really exhausting.

246
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:54,720
When will the seasons ever end?

247
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:57,000
Three meals of barbecue a day.

248
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:03,040
Who's calling?

249
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:04,720
Who is it?

250
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:05,560
It's Yiran.

251
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:08,720
You take it, you take it.

252
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:09,520
Okay.

253
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,080
Hello? What's up?

254
00:16:13,280 --> 00:16:15,840
Wu Huilan, I've told you so many times.

255
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:18,040
You need to put your toothbrush back after using it.

256
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:19,520
Or else you won't find it next time.

257
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:21,200
Got it, got it.

258
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:21,800
And what about your...

259
00:16:21,800 --> 00:16:22,680
work uniform?

260
00:16:22,680 --> 00:16:24,120
Why is it in the bathroom?

261
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:25,400
My work uniform?

262
00:16:25,400 --> 00:16:26,880
My company issued us a new set.

263
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:27,680
I have something to wear.

264
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:28,480
Don't worry about it.

265
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:30,800
Why is it so noisy over there?

266
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:33,320
I... I... I...

267
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:34,880
I'm in the bathroom.

268
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:36,560
Someone next to me is washing their hands.

269
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:37,600
They're waiting for me to give them a massage.

270
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:38,080
Alright, alright.

271
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:39,040
I'll hang up now.

272
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:40,160
A massage? You...

273
00:16:43,760 --> 00:16:45,200
Every single one of them

274
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:46,800
hangs up before I can even finish speaking.

275
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:48,280
So rude.

276
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:52,640
Are you really not going to

277
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:55,080
tell Yiran that you lost your job?

278
00:16:55,400 --> 00:16:56,560
What is there to say?

279
00:16:56,560 --> 00:16:58,720
She's going back to Shanghai next week anyway.

280
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:02,680
I'll just drift wherever life takes me.

281
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:04,160
Yiran is still young.

282
00:17:04,720 --> 00:17:06,440
A bright future is waiting for her.

283
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:11,800
My job loss has to stay a secret.

284
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:13,560
Make sure you don't let it slip.

285
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:14,440
Don't worry.

286
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:15,560
My lips

287
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:17,280
are sealed tight.

288
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:18,760
I'm so annoyed.

289
00:17:19,360 --> 00:17:20,800
Grab me a beer.

290
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:23,040
You promised Yiran you'd stop drinking.

291
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:25,600
If you get drunk, how will you explain it to her?

292
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:30,720
Just one glass.

293
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:44,760
Look at this sky.

294
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,320
It's exactly like my mood.

295
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:53,680
It comes and goes just like that.

296
00:17:57,960 --> 00:17:58,840
Yiran,

297
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:01,840
are you really planning to go back to Shanghai?

298
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:04,960
Yeah.

299
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:06,720
It's a rare opportunity.

300
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:08,360
Wu Huilan found a job too,

301
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:10,320
so it's about time I headed back.

302
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:13,520
I don't want you to go.

303
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:15,280
Once you leave,

304
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:17,440
who knows when you'll be back next.

305
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:18,960
For the New Year!

306
00:18:19,080 --> 00:18:20,640
I'll definitely come back for the New Year.

307
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,080
Don't lie to me.

308
00:18:22,080 --> 00:18:22,960
Really.

309
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:25,320
A lone shadow on the cold river,

310
00:18:25,320 --> 00:18:26,720
an old friend in the martial world.

311
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:28,640
Meeting by chance, why must we have met before?

312
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:32,480
Chen Baixi,

313
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:34,520
why are you being so sentimental?

314
00:18:34,520 --> 00:18:36,200
Are you afraid I'll run off without paying you?

315
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:38,000
How is that possible?

316
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:41,160
I never planned to ask you for that money.

317
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:43,480
What's mine is mine.

318
00:18:44,280 --> 00:18:45,440
Once I return to Shanghai,

319
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:48,080
our debt will be paid off soon.

320
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:54,360
Yo, bro.

321
00:18:54,360 --> 00:18:55,600
Nice acting this time.

322
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:58,320
I could even see the reluctance to part in your eyes.

323
00:19:00,320 --> 00:19:03,000
After all, Xiaoxitian is losing half its sky.

324
00:19:08,800 --> 00:19:10,120
Bro.

325
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:10,960
In everything you do,

326
00:19:10,960 --> 00:19:12,600
you can't always rely on others.

327
00:19:12,720 --> 00:19:13,640
I believe

328
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:15,880
with you and Xiaofang working together,

329
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:17,680
Xiaoxitian will definitely get better and better.

330
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:21,400
Don't try to comfort me.

331
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:23,200
Everyone has their own ambitions.

332
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:24,760
Everyone has their own path to take.

333
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:29,760
Those involved are blind.

334
00:19:29,760 --> 00:19:31,400
Detachment brings wisdom.

335
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:32,880
Outsiders see things clearly.

336
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:34,640
Stop right there.

337
00:19:35,160 --> 00:19:37,720
I hate listening to you bookworms talk.

338
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:39,120
Speak like a normal person.

339
00:19:39,120 --> 00:19:40,360
Listening to you is exhausting.

340
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:42,880
But I just love listening to you talk.

341
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:46,040
I love listening to whatever you say, Chen Xiaofang.

342
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:47,160
Li Yiran,

343
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:48,520
you silly woman...

344
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:49,800
You just love saying these things.

345
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:50,960
But I really don't want you to go.

346
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:54,200
Come here.

347
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:55,360
Come here.

348
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:09,120
Recently,

349
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:12,040
police in many areas solved a major child trafficking case.

350
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:14,880
The criminal gang often pretended to ask for directions,

351
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:16,760
offer help, or give gifts

352
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:18,560
to approach children playing alone.

353
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:19,760
The police disclosed

354
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:21,200
that the gang was highly organized,

355
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:23,480
using fake plates to commit crimes across regions,

356
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:25,320
greatly increasing the difficulty of the investigation.

357
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:28,640
Station commentator and criminologist Professor Li noted

358
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:29,320
that such cases

359
00:20:29,320 --> 00:20:31,720
highlight the importance of guardianship in public spaces.

360
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:33,880
He also urged schools and communities to work together

361
00:20:33,880 --> 00:20:35,400
to raise awareness against trafficking

362
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:37,280
and make anti-trafficking education a regular practice.

363
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:39,480
Fucking human traffickers.

364
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:42,120
Their kids will definitely be born without assholes.

365
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:44,000
Huilan,

366
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:45,440
it's almost time to get off work.

367
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:48,160
Careful, your kid might see you.

368
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:52,360
What are you laughing at?

369
00:20:52,360 --> 00:20:54,280
What's so funny? Seriously.

370
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:55,840
If my Yiran finds me,

371
00:20:55,840 --> 00:20:56,800
like you guys said,

372
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:57,600
me, I'll just...

373
00:20:58,280 --> 00:20:59,400
I know!

374
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:00,880
"Tear my mouth wide open!"

375
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:03,800
My ears have calluses from hearing it!

376
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:06,520
Xi Wa!

377
00:21:07,080 --> 00:21:08,560
Time to go home!

378
00:21:09,040 --> 00:21:10,320
Xi Wa!

379
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:16,840
Where did you go?

380
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,400
Why won't you listen?

381
00:21:22,560 --> 00:21:24,640
Go home with Grandma.

382
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:32,600
Xi Wa!

383
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:35,440
Where did you go?

384
00:21:36,840 --> 00:21:37,680
What's wrong with her?

385
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:39,760
The old lady's grandson,

386
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:42,440
was lost here twenty years ago.

387
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:44,440
So pitiful.

388
00:21:48,120 --> 00:21:50,040
These human traffickers really are...

389
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:53,400
Me, if I caught them, I'd slice them to pieces,

390
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:54,040
chop them up,

391
00:21:54,040 --> 00:21:54,840
and feed them to the dogs!

392
00:21:55,240 --> 00:21:56,440
If you ask me,

393
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:57,320
the ones left alive

394
00:21:57,880 --> 00:21:58,880
suffer even more.

395
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:00,520
That's true.

396
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:00,920
Look,

397
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:03,080
look at her, she's so pitiful.

398
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:05,280
She's so old and all alone.

399
00:22:05,280 --> 00:22:07,520
Grandma can't find you!

400
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:16,040
Xi Wa!

401
00:22:16,680 --> 00:22:17,920
Go home!

402
00:22:18,520 --> 00:22:19,360
So pitiful.

403
00:22:22,760 --> 00:22:23,480
What time is it?

404
00:22:23,480 --> 00:22:24,360
I'm leaving.

405
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:27,000
It's still early.

406
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:29,600
Getting off work soon. Gotta go, gotta go.

407
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:30,400
Hang out a bit longer.

408
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:31,240
Just a bit longer.

409
00:22:31,240 --> 00:22:32,000
No, I'm done.

410
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:32,880
You two chat.

411
00:22:34,520 --> 00:22:36,840
Yangyang, let's go home.

412
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:38,240
Huilan.

413
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:40,000
What a cute fishy!

414
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:41,200
I want it.

415
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:42,160
You want it?

416
00:22:42,680 --> 00:22:43,280
Sure.

417
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:44,840
Boss!

418
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:46,200
Come here for a second.

419
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:46,640
Okay.

420
00:22:47,040 --> 00:22:47,920
Get a fish for us.

421
00:22:48,520 --> 00:22:49,280
Which one do you want?

422
00:22:49,840 --> 00:22:50,880
That one.

423
00:22:51,280 --> 00:22:52,280
All right, this one.

424
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:53,520
Here.

425
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:04,720
What are you afraid of?

426
00:23:06,040 --> 00:23:08,880
These fish are raised to be killed and eaten.

427
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:10,120
But Yaya...

428
00:23:11,920 --> 00:23:12,760
Yaya can't be eaten.

429
00:23:12,760 --> 00:23:13,920
Yaya can't be eaten.

430
00:23:13,920 --> 00:23:15,320
Yaya is a pet.

431
00:23:15,320 --> 00:23:16,800
Yaya is meant to be kept.

432
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:18,520
This kind of fish is meant to be eaten.

433
00:23:20,280 --> 00:23:20,960
All right, all right.

434
00:23:20,960 --> 00:23:22,440
If you're scared to look, just turn around.

435
00:23:30,600 --> 00:23:33,560
Yangyang, listen to your godmother.

436
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:36,400
Being scared is useless.

437
00:23:39,160 --> 00:23:40,240
A lot of things,

438
00:23:41,040 --> 00:23:43,160
just because you like them,

439
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:44,880
doesn't mean they'll stay with you forever.

440
00:23:45,480 --> 00:23:47,040
Just like your mom and me,

441
00:23:48,440 --> 00:23:49,800
we both will get old.

442
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:52,680
We can't stay by your side forever.

443
00:23:52,680 --> 00:23:53,760
Once you grow up,

444
00:23:54,800 --> 00:23:56,840
you have to learn to face things yourself.

445
00:23:56,840 --> 00:23:58,040
You need to be a bit braver.

446
00:23:58,280 --> 00:23:59,160
Got it?

447
00:24:18,040 --> 00:24:19,480
There, there.

448
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:22,040
Come here, give your godmother a hug.

449
00:24:22,520 --> 00:24:24,480
You're so silly. Why are you crying?

450
00:24:26,240 --> 00:24:27,680
There, stop crying.

451
00:24:27,680 --> 00:24:28,200
Sweetie.

452
00:24:35,520 --> 00:24:36,760
Here's some tea for your dad.

453
00:24:37,160 --> 00:24:38,120
My dad said...

454
00:24:38,320 --> 00:24:39,600
they're this year's...

455
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:40,760
first harvest.

456
00:24:48,720 --> 00:24:51,120
You know quite a lot about tea.

457
00:24:51,520 --> 00:24:53,200
I recognize this box.

458
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:54,280
It's a lychee vine pattern.

459
00:24:55,800 --> 00:24:56,400
Right.

460
00:24:56,960 --> 00:24:59,360
It symbolizes endless life...

461
00:24:59,360 --> 00:25:00,920
and prosperity.

462
00:25:02,080 --> 00:25:03,400
They print this on urns, too.

463
00:25:05,760 --> 00:25:06,680
What...

464
00:25:06,680 --> 00:25:07,800
What do you mean by that?

465
00:25:09,360 --> 00:25:10,400
However...

466
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:12,280
it's a bit heavier than an urn.

467
00:25:12,680 --> 00:25:13,560
The material is quite nice.

468
00:25:14,560 --> 00:25:15,440
We are...

469
00:25:15,440 --> 00:25:16,680
on a blind date.

470
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:17,960
How could you say...

471
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:19,840
this is an urn?

472
00:25:27,080 --> 00:25:28,320
Why are you crying?

473
00:25:31,240 --> 00:25:32,040
Here, here.

474
00:25:37,840 --> 00:25:39,480
Xiao... Xiaofang?

475
00:25:39,720 --> 00:25:41,880
Your conversation is so touching.

476
00:25:47,320 --> 00:25:48,120
Please, continue.

477
00:25:50,280 --> 00:25:51,280
We're on a blind date.

478
00:25:51,720 --> 00:25:52,360
Who are you?

479
00:25:53,080 --> 00:25:54,480
So you're on a blind date.

480
00:25:55,040 --> 00:25:56,280
My apologies, I'm sorry.

481
00:25:56,400 --> 00:25:58,280
If I may ask...

482
00:25:58,280 --> 00:26:00,280
do you two have any...

483
00:26:00,280 --> 00:26:01,320
plans to get married?

484
00:26:03,880 --> 00:26:05,480
We just met.

485
00:26:05,480 --> 00:26:07,800
We still need to get to know each other better.

486
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:10,160
Right. Who gets married on the first date?

487
00:26:10,160 --> 00:26:11,520
Getting to know him is easy.

488
00:26:11,520 --> 00:26:13,080
Just ask me.

489
00:26:13,080 --> 00:26:14,200
I'm his ex-wife.

490
00:26:15,360 --> 00:26:16,560
What?

491
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:17,600
You were married?

492
00:26:18,680 --> 00:26:19,480
Divorced.

493
00:26:21,320 --> 00:26:23,440
We're still in the divorce cooling-off period.

494
00:26:24,360 --> 00:26:25,560
Married and divorced?

495
00:26:25,560 --> 00:26:27,120
Why go on a blind date if you're married?!

496
00:26:27,320 --> 00:26:28,320
You scumbag!

497
00:26:34,360 --> 00:26:36,840
I'm on a blind date because I got divorced!

498
00:26:37,320 --> 00:26:38,360
So you really like blind dates?

499
00:26:39,120 --> 00:26:40,160
No.

500
00:26:40,160 --> 00:26:42,120
Xiaofang, you know me.

501
00:26:42,120 --> 00:26:43,600
I'm just doing this to appease my dad.

502
00:26:44,640 --> 00:26:45,440
No need to explain it to me.

503
00:26:45,440 --> 00:26:46,200
I don't want to hear it.

504
00:26:47,560 --> 00:26:49,920
Xiaofang, are you jealous?

505
00:26:53,480 --> 00:26:54,280
What a joke.

506
00:26:54,280 --> 00:26:55,840
Why would be jealous?

507
00:26:57,280 --> 00:26:59,160
Good. That's good.

508
00:26:59,880 --> 00:27:00,880
Young Master Zhou.

509
00:27:01,080 --> 00:27:02,480
You're quite capable now.

510
00:27:02,480 --> 00:27:04,720
Today you can go on a blind date to appease your dad...

511
00:27:04,920 --> 00:27:05,760
tomorrow,

512
00:27:05,760 --> 00:27:06,880
to fulfill your filial duty,

513
00:27:06,880 --> 00:27:08,200
you could kick me, Chen Xiaofang, out of the house.

514
00:27:09,080 --> 00:27:10,600
If I, Zhou Fang, were that kind of person...

515
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:12,560
I'd get hit by bird poop the moment I walk out!

516
00:27:12,600 --> 00:27:14,080
Why not swear to be struck by lightning?

517
00:27:14,520 --> 00:27:15,320
Wipe it yourself.

518
00:27:19,360 --> 00:27:20,480
Being struck by lightning works too!

519
00:27:21,320 --> 00:27:22,120
Xiaofang!

520
00:27:22,720 --> 00:27:23,800
Xiaofang!

521
00:27:24,360 --> 00:27:25,080
Xiao...

522
00:27:32,200 --> 00:27:34,400
I've never seen karma strike so fast.

523
00:27:37,120 --> 00:27:38,640
Don't swear oaths so recklessly from now on.

524
00:27:43,280 --> 00:27:45,840
This world has finally gone mad.

525
00:27:47,080 --> 00:27:48,960
Miss, care to check out our tour packages?

526
00:27:48,960 --> 00:27:51,320
Seven days and nights, originally 3,999.

527
00:27:51,320 --> 00:27:52,680
Now, it's only 99.

528
00:27:53,200 --> 00:27:54,160
It's a rare opportunity.

529
00:27:54,960 --> 00:27:56,160
This isn't a scam, is it?

530
00:27:56,520 --> 00:27:58,480
Don't worry, miss.

531
00:27:58,480 --> 00:28:00,520
We're a legitimate travel agency.

532
00:28:00,520 --> 00:28:01,760
All of our tour routes

533
00:28:01,760 --> 00:28:03,640
are carefully selected.

534
00:28:03,640 --> 00:28:04,880
Great landscapes,

535
00:28:04,880 --> 00:28:05,840
and a tour guide.

536
00:28:08,160 --> 00:28:09,960
If it really is 99,

537
00:28:10,560 --> 00:28:11,800
then that's not bad.

538
00:28:11,800 --> 00:28:12,640
In all my life,

539
00:28:12,640 --> 00:28:14,440
I've never gone on a proper trip.

540
00:28:14,440 --> 00:28:15,360
Here, sign me up.

541
00:28:15,360 --> 00:28:16,000
I'll sign up.

542
00:28:16,960 --> 00:28:17,640
I'll go too.

543
00:28:20,760 --> 00:28:21,760
Huilan, what a coincidence.

544
00:28:23,800 --> 00:28:24,600
Is it?

545
00:28:25,840 --> 00:28:27,160
I live right here.

546
00:28:28,920 --> 00:28:30,400
Just passing by.

547
00:28:31,720 --> 00:28:33,280
I happen to need a getaway too.

548
00:28:33,560 --> 00:28:35,240
So, we can go together.

549
00:28:35,520 --> 00:28:36,600
And look out for each other.

550
00:28:37,160 --> 00:28:37,560
Sign me up.

551
00:28:37,560 --> 00:28:38,440
You guys know each other?

552
00:28:38,440 --> 00:28:39,280
Since you know each other,

553
00:28:39,280 --> 00:28:39,800
join together.

554
00:28:39,920 --> 00:28:42,640
This is a seniors' tour.

555
00:28:42,640 --> 00:28:43,720
You want to join too?

556
00:28:43,920 --> 00:28:46,960
He's so handsome, romantic, and rich.

557
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:49,320
Huilan has really

558
00:28:49,320 --> 00:28:50,720
struck some dumb luck.

559
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:53,040
More like bad luck, if you ask me.

560
00:28:53,840 --> 00:28:55,600
With what he has to offer,

561
00:28:55,920 --> 00:28:57,840
he could get any young girl he wants.

562
00:28:58,320 --> 00:28:59,920
Why does he keep pestering Huilan?

563
00:29:00,360 --> 00:29:01,840
I think there's something fishy going on.

564
00:29:02,520 --> 00:29:03,080
No.

565
00:29:03,080 --> 00:29:04,280
I can pay for myself.

566
00:29:05,280 --> 00:29:06,920
I think you're a weasel greeting a chicken.

567
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:08,240
You're up to no good.

568
00:29:08,440 --> 00:29:09,280
You...

569
00:29:09,280 --> 00:29:10,080
Wang Daren!

570
00:29:10,960 --> 00:29:12,280
Who are you calling a chicken?

571
00:29:12,880 --> 00:29:13,720
I...

572
00:29:15,440 --> 00:29:16,720
That's not what I meant.

573
00:29:16,720 --> 00:29:18,200
I definitely didn't mean you.

574
00:29:18,440 --> 00:29:19,920
I meant he's the weasel.

575
00:29:19,920 --> 00:29:22,120
Huilan, he just doesn't know how to talk.

576
00:29:22,120 --> 00:29:23,080
He meant that

577
00:29:23,360 --> 00:29:25,160
he's afraid you'll get tricked by the weasel.

578
00:29:26,560 --> 00:29:27,520
99 bucks, right?

579
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:31,520
I'll go too. Keep the change.

580
00:29:34,320 --> 00:29:37,760
99 bucks for seven days and nights of fun?

581
00:29:37,760 --> 00:29:39,080
Five-star hotels

582
00:29:39,080 --> 00:29:40,200
and private chauffeurs?

583
00:29:40,840 --> 00:29:41,680
And you believed that?

584
00:29:42,200 --> 00:29:44,360
Why don't you just write 'I'm a scammer' on your face?

585
00:29:45,080 --> 00:29:46,360
We are not scammers.

586
00:29:46,360 --> 00:29:47,360
We're a legitimate travel agency.

587
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:49,720
You guys don't sound legitimate at all.

588
00:29:49,720 --> 00:29:50,920
No, let me tell you,

589
00:29:50,920 --> 00:29:52,600
there are tons of scammers like this nowadays.

590
00:29:52,600 --> 00:29:53,840
They either claim it's free

591
00:29:53,840 --> 00:29:54,960
or advertise something like 99 bucks.

592
00:29:54,960 --> 00:29:56,080
It seems very cheap,

593
00:29:56,080 --> 00:29:58,200
but they specifically target middle-aged folks like you.

594
00:29:58,240 --> 00:29:59,920
99 bucks for seven days and seven nights?

595
00:29:59,920 --> 00:30:01,240
That wouldn't even cover their transport costs.

596
00:30:03,400 --> 00:30:04,520
Did they already pay?

597
00:30:04,520 --> 00:30:05,240
Refund them immediately.

598
00:30:05,240 --> 00:30:06,400
Or I'll call the cops right now.

599
00:30:07,160 --> 00:30:08,800
Yeah, give us our money back.

600
00:30:08,800 --> 00:30:10,920
Seven days and nights is too long.

601
00:30:11,040 --> 00:30:11,840
I still have to work.

602
00:30:11,840 --> 00:30:13,800
I can't take that much time off.

603
00:30:13,800 --> 00:30:14,840
Come on, refund it, bro.

604
00:30:14,840 --> 00:30:15,640
Refund mine too.

605
00:30:15,640 --> 00:30:16,760
Refund it.

606
00:30:16,760 --> 00:30:17,320
Refund what?

607
00:30:17,320 --> 00:30:17,640
Hurry up.

608
00:30:17,640 --> 00:30:18,040
Refund it.

609
00:30:18,040 --> 00:30:18,600
I can't.

610
00:30:18,600 --> 00:30:19,440
Just refund it.

611
00:30:20,040 --> 00:30:21,840
Boss Jiang already paid for it a long time ago.

612
00:30:22,160 --> 00:30:22,880
What?

613
00:30:30,400 --> 00:30:32,480
You really are a flirtatious weasel.

614
00:30:34,160 --> 00:30:35,560
No, don't get the wrong idea.

615
00:30:36,240 --> 00:30:36,920
Huilan.

616
00:30:37,280 --> 00:30:39,600
I actually just wanted to take you out to relax.

617
00:30:41,520 --> 00:30:42,680
Mr. Jiang, you...

618
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:44,600
Why are you taking her out to relax?

619
00:30:46,680 --> 00:30:48,480
Huilan lost her job.

620
00:30:50,280 --> 00:30:51,080
Yangyang!

621
00:30:51,240 --> 00:30:52,040
Shoo.

622
00:30:53,360 --> 00:30:54,160
What?

623
00:30:54,160 --> 00:30:56,120
Wu Huilan, you lost your job again?!

624
00:30:57,520 --> 00:30:58,440
No, I didn't.

625
00:30:58,440 --> 00:31:00,400
How could I possibly lose my job?

626
00:31:11,520 --> 00:31:13,160
Leniency for those who confess, severity for those who resist.

627
00:31:14,360 --> 00:31:16,040
You actually believe what Yangyang said?

628
00:31:17,200 --> 00:31:18,480
I'm Angel Baby.

629
00:31:18,520 --> 00:31:20,120
How could I possibly get fired?

630
00:31:20,120 --> 00:31:20,920
Angel Baby, my ass.

631
00:31:20,920 --> 00:31:22,000
Just tell me the truth.

632
00:31:22,280 --> 00:31:23,000
Tell you what?

633
00:31:23,200 --> 00:31:24,040
Where were you yesterday?

634
00:31:24,040 --> 00:31:24,840
At the shop.

635
00:31:25,040 --> 00:31:26,400
You left home at 7:00 a.m.

636
00:31:26,400 --> 00:31:28,600
Why do your WeChat steps only show 278?

637
00:31:28,600 --> 00:31:29,280
What the hell is this?

638
00:31:29,280 --> 00:31:30,160
How did you know?

639
00:31:30,520 --> 00:31:31,360
None of your business.

640
00:31:32,320 --> 00:31:33,040
Uncle Daren...

641
00:31:33,040 --> 00:31:33,800
He gave me a ride.

642
00:31:33,800 --> 00:31:34,640
He drove me there and back.

643
00:31:34,640 --> 00:31:35,600
I didn't walk.

644
00:31:35,920 --> 00:31:36,520
Where's your uniform?

645
00:31:36,800 --> 00:31:37,520
At the shop.

646
00:31:37,600 --> 00:31:38,840
It wasn't confiscated by the shop, right?

647
00:31:38,880 --> 00:31:39,720
How is that possible?

648
00:31:39,720 --> 00:31:40,960
I'll bring it back to show you tomorrow.

649
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:42,160
How much did you get paid this month?

650
00:31:42,160 --> 00:31:43,960
3,800. I already told you.

651
00:31:43,960 --> 00:31:45,240
3,800? I checked your bank statement.

652
00:31:45,240 --> 00:31:46,320
You didn't get paid at all.

653
00:31:46,520 --> 00:31:47,760
That's because the boss delayed my pay.

654
00:31:47,760 --> 00:31:48,840
I'll get it in a couple of days.

655
00:31:54,040 --> 00:31:54,840
Fine.

656
00:31:55,320 --> 00:31:56,680
What's the new shop next to Yunshui Pavilion?

657
00:31:57,240 --> 00:31:58,080
A bun shop.

658
00:31:58,520 --> 00:31:59,200
What's their specialty?

659
00:31:59,440 --> 00:32:00,360
Vermicelli buns.

660
00:32:00,720 --> 00:32:01,440
What drinks do they sell?

661
00:32:01,800 --> 00:32:02,520
Soy milk.

662
00:32:03,080 --> 00:32:04,360
Soy milk? Isn't it coffee?

663
00:32:04,680 --> 00:32:05,360
They have coffee, too.

664
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:06,320
Coffee, my ass.

665
00:32:06,320 --> 00:32:07,840
No shop opened at all. I was tricking you.

666
00:32:08,200 --> 00:32:09,000
You...

667
00:32:09,480 --> 00:32:10,600
Me, you set me up!

668
00:32:10,600 --> 00:32:11,520
Crazy.

669
00:32:12,280 --> 00:32:13,080
Still eating?

670
00:32:13,560 --> 00:32:14,320
Are you really that hungry?

671
00:32:14,320 --> 00:32:15,640
You still have an appetite after losing your job?

672
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:22,800
The reason?

673
00:32:25,440 --> 00:32:26,400
Spit it out.

674
00:32:27,920 --> 00:32:29,200
I reported the boss.

675
00:32:29,200 --> 00:32:30,240
You reported the boss?

676
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:31,120
Are you crazy?

677
00:32:31,400 --> 00:32:32,440
Crazy? Why would I be crazy?

678
00:32:32,960 --> 00:32:35,400
Son of a bitch. That client was a pervert.

679
00:32:35,400 --> 00:32:37,480
He was getting handsy with our technician.

680
00:32:37,480 --> 00:32:39,240
And our boss was an accomplice.

681
00:32:39,240 --> 00:32:40,840
He took that pervert's side.

682
00:32:41,080 --> 00:32:42,440
Me, you know my temper.

683
00:32:42,640 --> 00:32:44,760
I dragged them straight to the police station.

684
00:32:59,000 --> 00:33:00,400
I was wrong, okay?

685
00:33:00,400 --> 00:33:02,080
I shouldn't have meddled.

686
00:33:04,480 --> 00:33:05,640
This time, you were right to.

687
00:33:06,640 --> 00:33:07,440
You did good.

688
00:33:10,880 --> 00:33:11,840
What do you mean?

689
00:33:12,960 --> 00:33:15,280
What I mean is...

690
00:33:15,280 --> 00:33:16,680
You protected a coworker this time.

691
00:33:16,680 --> 00:33:17,680
You stood up for what's right.

692
00:33:17,680 --> 00:33:18,440
Great job.

693
00:33:19,880 --> 00:33:22,000
But from now on, which jobs you can take,

694
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,360
and which you can't,

695
00:33:23,360 --> 00:33:24,960
you need to use your best judgment, got it?

696
00:33:26,520 --> 00:33:28,320
Alright, eat up.

697
00:33:38,560 --> 00:33:39,880
What do you mean?

698
00:33:41,120 --> 00:33:43,800
It's so sour. Me, I've been sick of it for ages.

699
00:33:47,560 --> 00:33:48,360
Zhou Fang,

700
00:33:48,720 --> 00:33:49,960
I feel a bit bad asking this,

701
00:33:49,960 --> 00:33:51,840
but I'll just get straight to the point.

702
00:33:51,840 --> 00:33:52,560
Go ahead.

703
00:33:52,720 --> 00:33:54,200
I wanted to ask you

704
00:33:54,200 --> 00:33:56,200
if Wu Huilan could come work here.

705
00:33:56,320 --> 00:33:57,360
Any job will do.

706
00:33:58,760 --> 00:33:59,400
Who?

707
00:33:59,800 --> 00:34:00,800
Wu Huilan.

708
00:34:04,360 --> 00:34:05,640
Li Yiran,

709
00:34:05,640 --> 00:34:07,880
I've helped you with everything I could.

710
00:34:08,360 --> 00:34:10,120
Your mom is an industry jinx.

711
00:34:10,120 --> 00:34:11,400
You can't do this to me!

712
00:34:11,400 --> 00:34:12,320
She ruins every industry she works in.

713
00:34:12,320 --> 00:34:13,560
It's not like I don't know that.

714
00:34:13,560 --> 00:34:14,800
Young Boss Zhou!

715
00:34:14,800 --> 00:34:15,920
What do you mean?

716
00:34:16,040 --> 00:34:17,160
Say it to my face!

717
00:34:17,160 --> 00:34:18,640
Why are you badmouthing me behind my back?

718
00:34:19,080 --> 00:34:19,680
Wu Huilan.

719
00:34:19,800 --> 00:34:20,960
What did we just agree on?

720
00:34:20,960 --> 00:34:21,920
Go wait for me outside.

721
00:34:24,520 --> 00:34:25,960
I'm sorry, Auntie Huilan.

722
00:34:27,520 --> 00:34:28,320
Zhou Fang,

723
00:34:29,280 --> 00:34:31,240
I heard you were expanding your business,

724
00:34:31,240 --> 00:34:32,520
so you must need more hands, right?

725
00:34:32,960 --> 00:34:34,240
But I don't need your mom.

726
00:34:34,560 --> 00:34:36,440
Your mom is a professional mourner and brawler.

727
00:34:36,440 --> 00:34:37,600
What could she possibly do here?

728
00:34:37,600 --> 00:34:38,400
Be a cleaner!

729
00:34:38,400 --> 00:34:39,160
Sure.

730
00:34:40,200 --> 00:34:40,720
Well...

731
00:34:41,480 --> 00:34:42,360
I mean, Li Yiran,

732
00:34:42,880 --> 00:34:44,480
just to get your mom a job,

733
00:34:44,480 --> 00:34:46,560
you really threw away your principles.

734
00:34:47,440 --> 00:34:49,400
Then I'll just call Xiaofang.

735
00:34:49,440 --> 00:34:51,080
You can ask her about my principles.

736
00:34:51,080 --> 00:34:52,040
She can start immediately.

737
00:34:52,240 --> 00:34:53,240
Thanks, Zhou Fang.

738
00:34:53,240 --> 00:34:55,120
I owe you a big favor, and I'll definitely repay you.

739
00:34:57,440 --> 00:35:00,120
But let me be clear up front.

740
00:35:00,240 --> 00:35:03,040
She has to follow the company rules.

741
00:35:03,280 --> 00:35:04,720
Whether she can stay or not

742
00:35:04,720 --> 00:35:06,360
depends entirely on Auntie Huilan herself.

743
00:35:06,360 --> 00:35:07,120
Of course, of course.

744
00:35:07,320 --> 00:35:10,200
I just came to get her an interview.

745
00:35:10,200 --> 00:35:11,640
Then,

746
00:35:11,640 --> 00:35:12,960
about Xiaofang and me...

747
00:35:13,160 --> 00:35:15,880
Don't worry. I'll put in a good word for you.

748
00:35:16,240 --> 00:35:16,840
Wu Huilan!

749
00:35:17,280 --> 00:35:17,960
Here!

750
00:35:18,520 --> 00:35:19,720
About your job,

751
00:35:19,720 --> 00:35:20,960
we can't waste a single minute.

752
00:35:21,480 --> 00:35:22,480
I'll leave her to you.

753
00:35:22,480 --> 00:35:23,520
I'm going to find Xiaofang.

754
00:35:24,520 --> 00:35:25,120
I'm off.

755
00:35:28,400 --> 00:35:29,160
Young Boss Zhou.

756
00:35:29,560 --> 00:35:30,120
Hello.

757
00:35:31,320 --> 00:35:32,040
Um...

758
00:35:34,880 --> 00:35:36,360
I even brought my apron.

759
00:35:36,640 --> 00:35:38,360
I can start as a cleaner.

760
00:35:38,400 --> 00:35:40,400
You're going to be a cleaner anyway.

761
00:35:40,640 --> 00:35:41,480
What were you thinking?

762
00:35:41,920 --> 00:35:43,920
Go polish all the shoes in the shop first.

763
00:35:49,160 --> 00:35:49,960
Shining shoes.

764
00:35:51,160 --> 00:35:53,480
Fine. Me, I've done it all.

765
00:35:53,800 --> 00:35:54,920
Shining shoes is nothing.

766
00:35:59,080 --> 00:35:59,760
288,000!

767
00:36:00,080 --> 00:36:01,720
My mom said not a penny less.

768
00:36:01,920 --> 00:36:02,920
Your mom gave me 188,000.

769
00:36:02,920 --> 00:36:03,840
What does she take me for?

770
00:36:06,160 --> 00:36:07,600
A few days ago, because of this,

771
00:36:07,600 --> 00:36:08,440
my mom was hospitalized!

772
00:36:08,960 --> 00:36:10,480
Didn't we go over budget on the renovations?

773
00:36:10,480 --> 00:36:12,640
Please, you two, calm down.

774
00:36:12,640 --> 00:36:13,800
Don't be mad, don't be mad.

775
00:36:13,920 --> 00:36:15,960
Within my limited scope of responsibilities,

776
00:36:15,960 --> 00:36:16,960
I'll throw in a package deal for you.

777
00:36:16,960 --> 00:36:17,840
You shut up!

778
00:36:18,800 --> 00:36:19,600
Okay.

779
00:36:20,840 --> 00:36:22,160
If your family doesn't give me the bride price now,

780
00:36:22,160 --> 00:36:23,400
I'm not getting married!

781
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:25,080
Then don't!

782
00:36:25,400 --> 00:36:26,400
Just to buy a house,

783
00:36:26,560 --> 00:36:28,400
we've already spent all our family's savings!

784
00:36:28,400 --> 00:36:29,760
For this 188,000 bride price,

785
00:36:29,760 --> 00:36:31,880
my parents had to beg and borrow everywhere!

786
00:36:32,200 --> 00:36:33,440
Are you trying to drive my family to death?

787
00:36:33,440 --> 00:36:35,160
Are you trying to drive me to death now?

788
00:36:35,680 --> 00:36:37,880
What's with the yelling? Are you cockfighting?

789
00:36:38,320 --> 00:36:39,200
Who are you?

790
00:36:41,440 --> 00:36:43,040
Are you two collecting debts?

791
00:36:43,040 --> 00:36:44,240
Or are you asking for a bride price?

792
00:36:44,240 --> 00:36:45,160
None of your damn business!

793
00:36:46,120 --> 00:36:47,560
I'm so sorry, you two.

794
00:36:47,560 --> 00:36:49,560
This is our company's new cleaning lady.

795
00:36:50,440 --> 00:36:52,240
Leave now. You don't have a say here.

796
00:36:52,960 --> 00:36:54,520
I really can't listen to this anymore.

797
00:36:54,840 --> 00:36:55,640
It's so frustrating!

798
00:36:57,240 --> 00:36:58,360
You two, turn around.

799
00:36:58,520 --> 00:37:00,320
Your mom, his mom.

800
00:37:00,520 --> 00:37:02,280
Are your two moms getting married,

801
00:37:02,280 --> 00:37:03,400
or are you two getting married?

802
00:37:04,080 --> 00:37:04,960
Your mom...

803
00:37:04,960 --> 00:37:06,080
Your mom...

804
00:37:07,640 --> 00:37:08,680
Don't swear.

805
00:37:08,720 --> 00:37:09,640
Don't fight.

806
00:37:13,320 --> 00:37:14,560
Come here for a sec, sis.

807
00:37:16,720 --> 00:37:18,040
Calm down, calm down.

808
00:37:18,040 --> 00:37:19,240
Calm down.

809
00:37:20,240 --> 00:37:22,840
On your big day, why are you pouting?

810
00:37:23,480 --> 00:37:26,600
Let me ask you. Do you want to marry him,

811
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:28,360
or do you just want his money?

812
00:37:28,560 --> 00:37:29,600
My mom said,

813
00:37:30,280 --> 00:37:31,960
if the money isn't right, the attitude isn't right.

814
00:37:31,960 --> 00:37:33,600
If the attitude isn't right, the person isn't right.

815
00:37:35,000 --> 00:37:37,080
Marriage is about two people living together.

816
00:37:37,520 --> 00:37:39,680
It's not a business deal with a scale.

817
00:37:40,080 --> 00:37:41,360
You're asking him for so much bride price,

818
00:37:41,360 --> 00:37:42,200
then let me ask you,

819
00:37:42,320 --> 00:37:44,280
how much dowry did your family prepare for you?

820
00:37:44,360 --> 00:37:45,800
My family prepared 88,000.

821
00:37:48,640 --> 00:37:49,440
Come here

822
00:37:50,160 --> 00:37:51,880
Come over, sit down

823
00:37:52,680 --> 00:37:53,480
Young man,

824
00:37:54,200 --> 00:37:55,280
this dowry

825
00:37:55,400 --> 00:37:56,880
is the bride's family's backing,

826
00:37:57,200 --> 00:37:58,360
and this bride price

827
00:37:58,520 --> 00:38:00,160
is the respect from the groom's family.

828
00:38:00,200 --> 00:38:02,560
Whether it's the bride price or the dowry,

829
00:38:02,840 --> 00:38:04,960
they both represent the parents' goodwill.

830
00:38:05,160 --> 00:38:07,440
It's their hope that after you two get married,

831
00:38:07,720 --> 00:38:09,520
you will live a good life together.

832
00:38:10,080 --> 00:38:11,200
Here's what I think.

833
00:38:11,600 --> 00:38:12,720
The bride price is 88,000.

834
00:38:13,280 --> 00:38:14,560
The dowry is 88,000.

835
00:38:14,960 --> 00:38:16,280
Both families prosper together.

836
00:38:17,360 --> 00:38:19,960
As for the rest, when you have a baby in the future,

837
00:38:20,080 --> 00:38:22,680
you can make up the difference at the one-month celebration.

838
00:38:23,280 --> 00:38:25,120
It's truly not easy being parents.

839
00:38:25,120 --> 00:38:25,880
Right?

840
00:38:26,200 --> 00:38:27,600
Why make it hard for everyone?

841
00:38:27,600 --> 00:38:29,080
This way, everyone is happy.

842
00:38:29,080 --> 00:38:29,840
Isn't that right?

843
00:38:32,480 --> 00:38:34,040
I think what she said makes a lot of sense.

844
00:38:35,880 --> 00:38:37,760
Honey, whatever you say goes.

845
00:38:39,480 --> 00:38:40,280
Young man,

846
00:38:40,280 --> 00:38:42,200
you must make up the rest of the dowry later.

847
00:38:42,800 --> 00:38:45,440
Otherwise, Auntie here will be the first to raise hell with your family.

848
00:38:45,800 --> 00:38:46,640
Don't worry, sis.

849
00:38:46,640 --> 00:38:47,960
I'll go tell my mom right now.

850
00:38:48,640 --> 00:38:49,400
Come back.

851
00:38:51,000 --> 00:38:52,560
Then you'll have to get me another wedding dress.

852
00:38:53,520 --> 00:38:55,920
Sure, that's a very simple request.

853
00:38:56,040 --> 00:38:56,840
What is your name?

854
00:38:56,840 --> 00:38:58,080
Go arrange it for them quickly.

855
00:38:58,160 --> 00:38:59,840
Whatever you like, as many dresses as you want.

856
00:38:59,840 --> 00:39:00,440
Xu Wumei.

857
00:39:00,440 --> 00:39:01,600
Just go when you're told to.

858
00:39:03,400 --> 00:39:04,920
Then please step this way, you two.

859
00:39:04,920 --> 00:39:06,720
Go straight ahead and turn right.

860
00:39:07,240 --> 00:39:08,000
Thank you, sis.

861
00:39:08,000 --> 00:39:08,520
No problem at all.

862
00:39:08,520 --> 00:39:09,120
This way, please.

863
00:39:09,120 --> 00:39:10,520
Go on, hurry up.

864
00:39:10,680 --> 00:39:11,600
She's so nice.

865
00:39:12,120 --> 00:39:13,120
Just you wait.

866
00:39:13,840 --> 00:39:14,640
Auntie Huilan.

867
00:39:15,280 --> 00:39:16,200
Boss Zhou.

868
00:39:16,920 --> 00:39:19,280
I see you really have a way with words.

869
00:39:21,800 --> 00:39:23,040
You're not suited for cleaning.

870
00:39:24,200 --> 00:39:26,040
From now on, you will be our company's

871
00:39:26,040 --> 00:39:27,360
marriage consultant.

872
00:39:28,760 --> 00:39:30,240
What's a marriage consultant?

873
00:39:31,080 --> 00:39:31,880
A matchmaker.

874
00:39:32,120 --> 00:39:32,920
Matchmaker?

875
00:39:33,600 --> 00:39:34,520
What do you mean, matchmaker?

876
00:39:35,120 --> 00:39:36,280
Me? I'm a marriage consultant.

877
00:39:36,280 --> 00:39:37,040
Got it?

878
00:39:38,040 --> 00:39:39,240
What marriage consultant?

879
00:39:39,240 --> 00:39:40,520
Why does marriage need a consultant?

880
00:39:40,720 --> 00:39:42,120
It sounds like a scam.

881
00:39:44,760 --> 00:39:46,040
In this world,

882
00:39:46,240 --> 00:39:48,080
you create your own title.

883
00:39:48,840 --> 00:39:49,640
This time around,

884
00:39:50,280 --> 00:39:52,240
Me, I'm definitely going to shine.

885
00:39:52,240 --> 00:39:53,200
Work hard.

886
00:39:53,880 --> 00:39:55,080
You can go back to Shanghai with peace of mind.

887
00:39:55,600 --> 00:39:57,440
I won't lose my job again.

888
00:39:58,520 --> 00:40:00,160
As long as you don't get fired,

889
00:40:00,160 --> 00:40:02,120
I'll be thanking the heavens.

890
00:40:02,240 --> 00:40:03,600
As long as you don't get fired,

891
00:40:03,600 --> 00:40:05,640
I'll be thanking the heavens.

892
00:40:07,800 --> 00:40:09,120
Before you go, there's a job.

893
00:40:09,120 --> 00:40:10,240
I'll send you the address.

894
00:40:10,240 --> 00:40:12,280
Tomorrow morning at 8:00. Be there or be square.

895
00:40:12,840 --> 00:40:13,800
Mr. Chen.

896
00:40:14,200 --> 00:40:15,080
Be there or be square.

897
00:40:15,360 --> 00:40:16,760
Before you go, there's a job.

898
00:40:16,800 --> 00:40:18,120
Tomorrow morning at 8:00.

899
00:40:18,120 --> 00:40:18,960
Be there or be square.

900
00:40:18,960 --> 00:40:20,880
You ignored the "job at 8:00" part

901
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:22,040
and only saw "be there or be square."

902
00:40:22,960 --> 00:40:24,240
I didn't notice.

903
00:40:24,960 --> 00:40:26,200
But then again, I think

904
00:40:26,680 --> 00:40:28,960
Mr. Chen is actually a pretty good guy.

905
00:40:28,960 --> 00:40:29,680
Just look at him.

906
00:40:29,680 --> 00:40:31,040
He's so tall,

907
00:40:31,400 --> 00:40:32,720
and he looks so sharp.

908
00:40:32,960 --> 00:40:34,680
If you get together with him in the future,

909
00:40:34,680 --> 00:40:35,840
get married, and have a baby,

910
00:40:35,840 --> 00:40:37,520
the kid would probably be quite pretty.

911
00:40:37,520 --> 00:40:38,680
Are you okay?

912
00:40:38,680 --> 00:40:40,040
I've told you a million times.

913
00:40:40,040 --> 00:40:41,560
Stop trying to play matchmaker.

914
00:40:41,880 --> 00:40:43,200
I'm an excellent judge of character.

915
00:40:43,840 --> 00:40:46,000
Besides, I'm a marriage consultant now. A professional.

916
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:47,040
You two

917
00:40:47,040 --> 00:40:49,080
kind of look like a couple.

918
00:40:54,800 --> 00:40:56,240
Really, really.

919
00:41:16,840 --> 00:41:19,400
It's not on them, and it's not at home.

920
00:41:20,160 --> 00:41:21,480
Where the hell is the bracelet?

921
00:41:46,840 --> 00:41:48,400
It was the same with the old man at the last place.

922
00:41:50,240 --> 00:41:52,000
He was dead for half a month before anyone noticed.

923
00:41:52,360 --> 00:41:54,240
It wasn't until the neighbors smelled the stench

924
00:41:54,240 --> 00:41:55,840
that they realized he was gone.

925
00:41:56,520 --> 00:41:58,720
His kids showed up just to look for cash and bankbooks.

926
00:41:59,920 --> 00:42:01,000
A bunch of ungrateful bastards.

927
00:42:02,000 --> 00:42:03,480
In this day and age,

928
00:42:05,440 --> 00:42:07,640
everyone is completely blinded by money.

929
00:42:30,720 --> 00:42:31,480
Mom.

930
00:42:31,480 --> 00:42:33,360
Where did you put the bracelet, Mom?

931
00:42:33,360 --> 00:42:33,920
Mr. Chen,

932
00:42:33,920 --> 00:42:34,520
this isn't right.

933
00:42:34,520 --> 00:42:35,320
What's wrong with it?

934
00:42:35,320 --> 00:42:36,120
She's my mom.

935
00:42:36,120 --> 00:42:37,160
Respect the dead.

936
00:42:38,880 --> 00:42:39,680
Let's go.

937
00:42:46,200 --> 00:42:47,760
Steady.

938
00:42:50,640 --> 00:42:53,520
Let the gongs and drums echo through the mountains.

939
00:42:54,240 --> 00:42:57,680
May white cranes guide your way to the West.

940
00:42:59,280 --> 00:43:02,120
Lay down the earthly toils of this life.

941
00:43:02,880 --> 00:43:06,120
May your path to the netherworld be free of storms.

942
00:43:07,320 --> 00:43:09,360
The police came last night.

943
00:43:09,360 --> 00:43:10,840
It's so tragic.

944
00:43:10,840 --> 00:43:11,800
Steady now.

945
00:43:11,800 --> 00:43:13,080
The hearse is right downstairs.

946
00:43:14,280 --> 00:43:15,400
How long has she been dead?

947
00:43:15,400 --> 00:43:16,240
I don't know.

948
00:43:17,080 --> 00:43:18,080
It's so tragic.

949
00:43:18,080 --> 00:43:19,040
She's been dead for a while.

950
00:43:19,040 --> 00:43:19,720
It smells awful.

951
00:43:19,720 --> 00:43:20,920
Her kid is so unfilial.

952
00:43:25,120 --> 00:43:27,080
Before your mother passed away,

953
00:43:27,080 --> 00:43:28,400
she made you some dumplings,

954
00:43:30,400 --> 00:43:31,240
and chili sauce.

955
00:44:13,560 --> 00:44:14,560
This bracelet...

956
00:44:16,120 --> 00:44:18,680
When my mom got married,

957
00:44:18,680 --> 00:44:20,280
my dad gave it to her.

958
00:44:20,880 --> 00:44:22,160
After my dad passed away,

959
00:44:22,520 --> 00:44:24,280
my mom raised me all by herself.

960
00:44:24,920 --> 00:44:28,840
After college, I was assigned to work in Qinghai.

961
00:44:30,440 --> 00:44:33,560
My mom didn't want to go that far with me.

962
00:44:34,720 --> 00:44:35,520
She said,

963
00:44:38,000 --> 00:44:40,680
she'd stay wherever my dad was.

964
00:44:41,560 --> 00:44:45,360
That bracelet was all she had left of my dad.

965
00:44:47,320 --> 00:44:51,600
I found this bracelet to bury it with her,

966
00:44:52,640 --> 00:44:53,800
so she and my dad

967
00:44:53,800 --> 00:44:55,200
could be buried together.

968
00:44:57,440 --> 00:44:58,920
We had a misunderstanding earlier.

969
00:44:58,920 --> 00:45:01,520
I thought once I made enough money,

970
00:45:02,280 --> 00:45:03,960
I could return home a success.

971
00:45:06,560 --> 00:45:07,360
But...

972
00:45:13,000 --> 00:45:14,200
I'm a failure.

973
00:45:14,440 --> 00:45:15,600
I'm a failure.

974
00:45:15,640 --> 00:45:16,840
I'm a failure.

975
00:45:17,880 --> 00:45:18,680
Sir...

976
00:45:20,400 --> 00:45:24,080
My mom... my mom never enjoyed a day of comfort.

977
00:45:25,160 --> 00:45:27,320
She never had a single good day.
